# Never bake into the image: secrets, local DBs, virtualenv, build artifacts.
# The build context is COPY'd into the image, so anything not excluded here
# ships inside every pushed layer (see docs/reviews/CODE_ANALYSIS_REPORT.md F-12).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-journal
# SQLite WAL sidecars: excluding `*.db` alone is not enough. WAL mode (on in
# dev and in the UI e2e harness) keeps the *live database content* in the
# -wal/-shm sidecars, so a multi-MB e2e WAL would ship the seeded users and
# events it was written for inside a distributed image layer.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# TLS material never ships inside an image layer (keys are secrets; the
# compose stack mounts the certs read-only at runtime instead).
*.key
*.crt
*.pem
infrastructure/nginx/certs/
data/
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
docs/
tests/
# Dev-only test harness — pytest is never run inside the image — plus
# regenerable audit/scan artifacts.
conftest.py
pytest.ini
ui_audit/
ui_maturity/
ui_e2e_artifacts_*/
.pw-browsers/
ui/node_modules/
*.egg-info/
.venv*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# BYOM: the image ships zero model weights — the operator mounts models/
# read-only at runtime (compose does this). Prevents an operator's local
# staging from leaking AGPL/research-restricted checkpoints into a layer.
models/staged/

# Customer-confidential business material (market research, competitor
# teardowns, pricing and phase plans). `COPY . /app` would otherwise bake the
# entire strategy folder into a distributed image layer. This entry is
# load-bearing: `roadmap/` is gitignored, so nothing else would stop it.
roadmap/
